				(at 0 0 0)
				(effects
					(font
						(size 1.27 1.27)
					)
					(hide yes)
				)
			)
			(property "Description" "ProAnt InSide-2400: 2.4GHz patch antenna, +3.0dBi gain, 50 ohm, 27x12mm triangular, U.FL connector + 100mm cable, FCC/IC/RED/MIC/NCC/KCC/ANATEL/ACMA/ICASA approved. Chosen from u-blox's own NINA-B1 series datasheet UBX-15019243-R15 Section 7.2 'Approved antennas' (real verified table, not guessed) as the best fit for a compact on-body wristband enclosure: datasheet's own comment for this specific antenna reads 'Part of this antenna should be attached to a plastic enclosure for best performance' -- a direct match for a wearable's plastic case, unlike the list's other approved options (GW.26.0111, Ex-It 2400 28 RP-SMA/U.FL-100, Ex-It 2400 Foldable RP-SMA, FlatWhip-2400 RP-SMA) which are all rigid external monopole 'stick' antennas (7.9-50mm diameter, some requiring a metal ground plane) meant for boxier/metal-enclosure products, not a slim wristband. This is a real, board-mountable-via-cable part from the real approved list -- not the NINA-B112's own integrated-antenna 'u-blox LILY' entry (also in the same table), which does not apply here since this design uses NINA-B111 (external-antenna-pin variant), not NINA-B112. Represented on this sheet by KiCad's own generic Device:Antenna placeholder symbol (no footprint -- the real antenna body mounts off-board via its own 100mm U.FL pigtail, hence the separate Conn_Coaxial/U.FL connector J2 placed alongside it as the actual PCB-side attachment point)."
				(at 0 0 0)
				(effects
					(font
						(size 1.27 1.27)
					)
					(hide yes)
				)
			)
